From f2b936b34d32a7a8a3b0807b15c852ef9673526d Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: build <build@localhost>
Date: Sat, 21 Nov 2026 08:43:49 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] Build ties that run along a staff line; give two ties into
 one note to the right heads

Long flat ties lie along a staff line: just above the top line or below the
bottom line (a whole note or a dotted half tied to the next note: Goodbye
Yellow Brick Road's and The Longest Time's left hands, Yellow Submarine's
right hand, Too Sweet's whole-note chords), or along a line inside the
staff. Close enough to merge with the line, they came out lost, though
their arcs were all in the skeleton.

The skeleton is computed on the image with its staff lines. Where the tie
touches the line, each vertical run holds both, and the skeleton runs in
its middle, a pixel or two off the tie towards the line, joined to the line
at both ends: the tie is cut into a free middle arc, merged stretches and
the free ends beyond the line. SlursBuilder could not join them again:
1. A merged stretch is flatter than the tie. Added to the middle arc, it
   gave a side model (the circle through three points of the last six
   interlines) bending the other way than the slur, a fraction of a pixel
   over a nearly straight side, and addArc refused the extension (ccw).
2. Where the extension was taken, the side model through the shifted points
   missed the points beyond it, and weed dropped the candidate (distance to
   the side model over 0.1 interline).
The middle arc alone ends two or more interlines short of the heads, so
ClumpPruner linked no head and no slur was kept: no curve at any step.

Now:
- SlurInfo.computeSideModel defines a side model by points moved back onto
  the curve (SlursBuilder.onCurve: where the run holding a staff line sticks
  out of it on one side only, by 0.1 interline or more, the curve's middle
  is half a line thickness inside the run's outer end), and computeImpacts
  measures a side model on those points too (sidePoints; a slur no longer
  than a side keeps its global model on the skeleton points).
- addArc lets an extension through when the new side model bends against
  the slur but is flat over its side (sagitta at most 0.07 interline:
  isFlat), unless the arc added is a piece of bare staff line, one interline
  or more, at least 4 points in 5 on a line with nothing sticking out
  (isAlongLine): a slur may not run on along a line.

Ties of a chord tied over the barline lie one above the other along the
lines, and two of them could be linked to the same two heads, nearest both
curve ends (Too Sweet's whole-note chords [D4 G4 Bb4 D5], Piano Man's
accordion [A3 C4 F4], Stumblin' In bar 5): the note between got none.
checkStaffTie now looks, when another curve links the very same heads, for
another pair right at this curve's ends (tieAlternativePair, as
tieAlternative sees one head: tie-compatible, not the end of another tie,
the space between clear) and moves the curve there; when both twins could
move, the one whose ends lie farther from the heads.

